<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osu Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Christiansborg Castle, Christiansborg, Fort Christiansborg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osu Castle, formerly Christiansborg, is a fort on the coast at Osu in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accra">Accra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>. Built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> from 1661 on land bought from the Ga, it was the headquarters of the Danish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> and a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> until it was sold to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1850. It later served as the seat of government of the Gold Coast and of Ghana.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osu-castle.jpg" alt="Osu Castle" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Twi inaccr · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osu_Castle_(also_known_as_Fort_Christiansborg_or_Christiansborg_Castle)_in_Accra,_Ghana.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
